# Drafted by Gemini (R26 White Worm), edited. The White Worm: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_worm_arrived
Narrator: Grey huts huddle along the shingle where old nets sag from every post, and pale worms gleam like peeled twigs in the dark shallows.
check Wisdom DC 17 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You hold tight to the names of those you love like warm stones in your pocket, and the water's hungry whisper slides harmlessly off your ears.
set mf_worm_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: You draw a breath of the damp lake mist and lose a whole quarter hour between one blink and the next, left only with a ringing skull and no notion why.
damage 2d10 psychic party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: You walk the wet stones of the shore as the mist curls into your mouth with the sharp, cold taste of old copper pennies.
time +60
check Wisdom DC 17 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
mf_pell_fisher [afraid]: We haul the nets up heavy with fat white worms every tide now, and a single splash of that water makes a man forget his own children's names.
set mf_worm_asked
quest mf_worm asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
mf_pell_fisher [weary]: Another whole family waded into the shallows at daybreak and came out staring like strangers, so tell me true if you bring any word of help.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_worm_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
mf_pell_fisher [afraid]: One swallow from the lake steals your mind for hours, swimming lets the worms burrow right under your skin, and those shore cultists swear they hear it singing.
-> menu

~ where
mf_pell_fisher [sad]: It does not belong to our waters at all, for that wicked hag Matron Lethica tore a hole from somewhere else and let it drop into the deep.
-> menu

~ route_a
mf_pell_fisher [neutral]: The first folk who lived by this water raised black stone obelisks along the bank, and their carvings might name what sleeps down there if you have the wit to read them.
* [Arcana DC 17] Decipher the black obelisks -> a_ok | a_slow
* [Investigation DC 17] Study the lake's first people's carvings -> a_ok | a_slow
* Copy every carving and puzzle at them for hours -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
mf_pell_fisher [smile]: Look there, those carvings are a plain warning once your eyes catch the shape of them, and they map the very rift where the creature spilled through.
time +60
set mf_worm_found
set mf_worm_clue_a
quest mf_worm trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: You spend a damp, squinting afternoon rubbing charcoal and copying the stone marks onto your sleeves until, by evening light, the crooked pattern finally speaks sense.
time +300
set mf_worm_found
quest mf_worm trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_lake_cultist [smile]: Welcome back to the water's edge, dear friends, have you heard our pale lord singing beneath the ripples yet, and will you lend your voices to our choir?
set mf_worm_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_lake_cultist [neutral]: The water keeps its patience and so do we, friends, so ask whatever still troubles your heavy minds.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_worm_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_worm_found and not flag.mf_worm_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_lake_cultist [sly]: The Great Worm sups on heavy memories, and we faithful are simply the blessed ones it has already tasted, gathering on the long jetty every midnight to sing.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_lake_cultist [sly]: Our humble Order is always glad of fresh throats on the planks, and truth be told, you only need to pretend you love the Worm well enough to fool the water.
* [Deception DC 17] Pretend to join the Worm's order -> b_ok | b_slow
* [Persuasion DC 17] Talk the cultists into taking you to the rift -> b_ok | b_slow
* Sit through the whole sermon and follow them out -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_lake_cultist [smile]: Oh, your sweet words make old Brother Silt weep for pure joy, so walk with our choir now as we lead you down the jetty to the rift!
time +60
set mf_worm_found
set mf_worm_clue_b
quest mf_worm trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: You endure a damp and unpleasantly winding sermon about the mercy of emptiness, though the choir does at last shuffle you down the creaking jetty toward the rift.
time +300
set mf_worm_found
quest mf_worm trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_lake_cultist [sly]: Listen close, the Worm dreads a single constellation painted by the lake's first folk, and if you hold that star sequence in your mind it will choke trying to swallow you.
* [Arcana DC 17] Work out the constellations from the obelisks -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [Nature DC 17] Chart the stars by the lake's reflection -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Trace the whole sky on the shore, star by star -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_lake_cultist [smile]: Mark those seven stars in their true order upon that scrap of oilcloth, and watch how the black water already flinches back from the shore.
time +60
give mf_star_chart
set mf_worm_weak
quest mf_worm ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: It takes the whole cold night lying belly-down on the shingle by the smoky glow of a shuttered lamp, but your star chart is inked and dry by dawn.
time +300
give mf_star_chart
set mf_worm_weak
quest mf_worm ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: Out past the rotting pilings of the long jetty, a jagged tear in the air hangs open above the black water while something vast and pale coils behind it.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_worm_reveals
Narrator: The White Worm heaves its bulk up from the split lake bed, vast and tallow-pale, its yawning mouth ringed with circles of soft, wet teeth.
cutscene mf_worm_reveals_2
Narrator: A low, boneless note hums from its gullet, and every small worm in the dark shallows swings its blind head toward you at once.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_worm_weak
combat mf_worm_weak
elif level >= 14
combat mf_worm_full
else
combat mf_worm_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_worm_falls
Narrator: The great pale bulk shudders, knots itself tight in sudden agony, and tumbles backward through the rift as the air seals shut behind it like a healing wound.
cutscene mf_worm_falls_2
Narrator: High above the quiet ripples, the leering crone in the moon rolls her heavy eye away from the water and fixes her gaze upon the dark timberline to the north.
cutscene end
set mf_worm_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give eye_of_the_white_worm
quest mf_worm slain
xp milestone
Narrator: Deep within Hartsblight Forest, the healed boughs are already bowing their crowns toward something tall that walks between the trunks.
-> END
